FiBA: On the Effectiveness of Invisible Backdoor Attacks in Federated Learning
Research implementation contributors: Matthijs Marinus and Vasileios Tsouvalas.
Paper authors: Matthijs Marinus, Vasileios Tsouvalas, and Nirvana Meratnia.

Recovered from vtsouval/fl_battacks at commit
77ee2a9208b909e9e83e24033f07a1338dc45756, originally under Apache-2.0.
That license is preserved in licenses/FiBA-Apache-2.0.txt. The combined source
release is distributed under GPL-3.0 because its WaNet adaptation contains
GPL-3.0 upstream code. Individual original contributions retain their applicable
Apache permissions; this does not relicense upstream code to Apache.

WaNet code in src/fiba/wanet.py adapts Anh Nguyen and Anh Tran's
Warping-based Backdoor Attack release. The historical GPL-3.0 source and license
were verified at upstream commit 94453080f241053ac7c8cc4717da20806ee17e5c:
https://github.com/VinAIResearch/Warping-based_Backdoor_Attack-release/tree/94453080f241053ac7c8cc4717da20806ee17e5c
The recovered FiBA WaNet implementation was first committed on 2024-02-26,
before upstream's July 2024 license change. This release uses that historical
GPL-3.0 implementation; it does not incorporate later AGPL revisions.

FoolsGold code in src/fiba/fools_gold.py adapts the implementation by Clement
Fung, Chris J. M. Yoon, and Ivan Beschastnikh, DistributedML/FoolsGold.
Its MIT license notice is preserved in licenses/FoolsGold-MIT.txt.
https://github.com/DistributedML/FoolsGold

BackdoorBox GPL-2.0 generator source is not included or imported by this
package. The LIRA adapter loads an independently supplied TorchScript artifact.
PCA/Lockdown source from upstream repositories without license grants is not
included. See PROVENANCE.md for changes and method limitations.
